From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:07:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ec/lenovo/h8: Give BAT1 a unique _UID

BAT0 and BAT1 are both control method batteries (PNP0C0A) with _UID 0.
ACPI requires _UID to be unique among devices with the same _HID, so
OSes may treat the two batteries as the same device.

Use _UID 1 for BAT1.

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541 and lenovo/x230.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl
index 0eb08ae0c..ca68cb1df 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl
@@ -371,7 +371,7 @@ Device (BAT0)
 Device (BAT1)
 {
 	Name (_HID, EisaId ("PNP0C0A"))
-	Name (_UID, 0x00)
+	Name (_UID, 0x01)
 	Name (_PCL, Package () { \_SB })
 
 	// Template for _BIF
-- 
2.43.0

